{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>You shall do no unrighteousness in judgment.</b> If this refers to judgment, is it not already stated ״לֹא תַעֲשׂוּ עָוֶל בַּמִּשְׁפָּט״ (verse 15)? What then is the מִּשְׁפָּט repeated here? It is the measure, the weight, and the volume. This teaches that one who measures is called a judge — for if he falsified the measure, it is as though he corrupted the judgment, and he is called an oppressor, hated and abominable, banned and an abomination, and he causes the five things stated concerning a judge: he defiles the land, and profanes the Name, and removes the Shechinah, and fells Israel by the sword, and exiles them from their land (Sifra)." "<b>In measure.</b> This is the dry measure (ibid.)." "<b>In weight.</b> As it sounds." "<b>And in volume.</b> It is the measure of liquid and dry (Bava Metzia 61a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:22.645082276Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}